{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0D13", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{section-deformations-ringed-spaces}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:091eda03c0bae80417d58741c821ff41990006bee9ee47004898ee5d6f88e736", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we spell out what the results in\nSection <REF_0001>\nmean for deformations of schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b74eeed8a0546629b8d33785efd3b8495676f6f92c1ce96f94f6b2393f7f3ca", "unit_id": "tag:0D13:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0D13", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\subset S'$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0004": "$a : X \\to X' \\times_{S'} S$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$(f' : X' \\to S', a)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Ext^1_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(\\NL_{X/S}, f^*\\mathcal{C}_{S/S'})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\varphi : X' \\to X'$", "MATH_0009": "$S'$", "MATH_0010": "$X' \\times_{S'} S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Ext^0_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(\\NL_{X/S}, f^*\\mathcal{C}_{S/S'})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-deform}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8dfa65c280d3933c4184ed3d78f9ea8eab13a1653c56dc611ca6d6089c9b4fa5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:99bf39f44c3cd645165cf201566be8e80fa4eb690216123f792bccd37111f946", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a first order thickening of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a flat morphism of schemes.\nIf there exists a flat morphism <MATH_0003> of schemes\nand an isomorphism <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>, then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the set of isomorphism classes of pairs <MATH_0006> is\nprincipal homogeneous under\n<MATH_0007>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the set of automorphisms of <MATH_0008>\nover <MATH_0009> which reduce to the identity on <MATH_0010>\nis <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f96d3b48d36b648071fe2d342a49fe1223c4eeba58cee6bb36ef19ececfd1405", "unit_id": "tag:0D14:statement"}
{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0D13", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X'$", "MATH_0003": "$(f, f') : (X \\subset X') \\to (S \\subset S')$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$X'$", "MATH_0006": "$f^*\\mathcal{C}_{S/S'}$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n0 \\ar[r] & f^*\\mathcal{C}_{S/S'} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{O}_{X'} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{O}_X \\ar[r] & 0 \\\\\n0 \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{C}_{S/S'} \\ar[u] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{O}_{S'} \\ar[u] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{O}_S \\ar[u] \\ar[r] & 0\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$\\NL_{X/S}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\NL_{X/S}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-thickenings}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-thickenings-spaces}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-deform}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-deform-module}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{equation-to-solve-ringed-spaces}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-choices-ringed-spaces}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-huge-diagram-ringed-spaces}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-netherlander}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{section-deformations-ringed-spaces}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:27cc4876d6ef57ad8f71dabebb88c759e598930d02e134b0038f2103b0ec2ad9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:29703a591c4268232f6e435930ccfec088e12f721fbf52cac468f90186e00c17", "source_text": "First we observe that thickenings of schemes as defined in\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0001>\nare the same things as morphisms of schemes which\nare thickenings in the sense of\nSection <REF_0002>.\nWe may think of <MATH_0001> as a closed subscheme of <MATH_0002>\nso that <MATH_0003>\nis a morphism of first order thickenings. Then we see\nfrom More on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0003>\n(or from the more general Lemma <REF_0004>)\nthat the ideal sheaf of <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005> is equal to <MATH_0006>.\nHence we have a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0007>\nwhere the vertical arrows are <MATH_0008>-maps; please compare with\n(<REF_0005>).\nThus part (1) follows from\nLemma <REF_0006>\nand part (2) from part (2) of\nLemma <REF_0007>.\n(Note that <MATH_0009> as defined for a morphism of schemes in\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0008>\nagrees with <MATH_0010> as used in\nSection <REF_0009>.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:165f1406fe39f72c9aa3806f43f6a556ff178b6d4c6df6cb74d26194ddd2692c", "unit_id": "tag:0D14:proof"}
